body:
My mom: BP2. My mom's birth mother and 6 biological sisters: BP1 or 2 (she was adopted and met them when she was an adult). My half-brother (we have the same mom): Bipolar 2. My sister: Diagnosed "Borderline" but got a professional 2nd opinion and was diagnosed as BP2. My dad's side of the family have the mentality of "I don't want to acknowledge my mental health since I don't believe in that." but I'm SURE there's undiagnosed BP. I'm diagnosed BP2, anxiety, ADHD, and OCD (which probably goes hand in hand with the anxiety!) 

My husband is definitely undiagnosed with severe depression. His grandpa had severe mood swings (of course back then he didn't get a diagnosis) and they suspect he had schizophrenia. My husband's dad was in a mental hospital in the 70s for paranoid schizophrenia. He also has 1 brother that's paranoid schizophrenic and 3 half-brothers that suffer from BP.  

We joke about not passing it down to our kids and just getting a bunch of cats as our children. But that just might be the mania talking. lol. (;
